;; The air-crew appview Worker. :esm, mirroring cloud-itonami-marketplace-listing
;; and app-ongakuka.
;;
;; wrangler.jsonc's main points at dist/worker.js, which is THIS bundle compiled
;; from the source in src/. That is the whole point of the migration recorded in
;; docs/adr/0001: before it, main pointed at a SvelteKit build output that is not
;; in the tree, and the TypeScript a reader opened was in no bundle at all.
;;
;; :warnings-as-errors lives inside :compiler-options ON PURPOSE. shadow-cljs
;; treats an undeclared or renamed var as a WARNING and still exits 0, shipping a
;; bundle that throws on its first request -- a green build is not a check.
;; Putting the key under :build-options instead is worse than not having it:
;; shadow ignores it there silently, so the safeguard reads as present while
;; being inert. That misplacement is itself a check that cannot fail, which is
;; the class of defect this repo's gates exist to catch. scripts/verify-docs-claims.cljs
;; PARSES this file as EDN and asserts the key's position -- it does not grep,
;; because this very comment contains the string.
{:deps {:aliases [:cljs]}
 :builds
 {:worker
  {:target :esm
   :output-dir "dist"
   :modules {:worker {:exports {default air-crew.worker/handler}}}
   :compiler-options {:output-feature-set :es2020
                      :infer-externs :auto
                      :warnings-as-errors true}}}}
